## 9. Binary Search

```python
nums = list(map(int, input("Enter numbers: ").split()))
key = int(input("Enter key: "))

nums.sort()

low = 0
high = len(nums) - 1
found = False

while low <= high:
    mid = (low + high) // 2

    if nums[mid] == key:
        print("Element found at position", mid + 1)
        found = True
        break
    elif nums[mid] < key:
        low = mid + 1
    else:
        high = mid - 1

if not found:
    print("Element not found")

print("Time Complexity: O(log n)")
```
